WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.730
- One of the peculiar things

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.120
about us human beings,

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.970
is our mortality.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.880
Ernest Becker explored it in general.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.140
Do you ponder the value of mortality?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.123
Do you think about your own mortality?

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.464
- I used to, when I
was about 12 years old.

00:00:18.464 --> 00:00:19.779
(laughing)

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:21.220
I wondered.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.610
I didn't care much about my own mortality,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:24.750
but I was worried about

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.070
the fact that if my consciousness

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.990
disappeared would the
entire universe disappear.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.280
That was frightening.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.440
- Did you ever find an
answer to that question?

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.600
- No, nobody's ever found an answer.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.600
But I stopped being bothered by it.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.830
It's kinda like Woody Allen,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.090
and one of his films.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.884
You may recall,

00:00:43.884 --> 00:00:45.800
it starts when he goes to a shrink

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.790
when he's a child,

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.177
and the shrink asks him,

00:00:48.177 --> 00:00:49.230
"What's your problem?"

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.140
and he says, "I just learned that

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.390
the universe is expanding.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:54.723
I can't handle that."

00:00:54.723 --> 00:00:56.300
(laughing)

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.940
- And then another absurd question is,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.100
what do you think is the meaning

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.310
of our existence here?

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.210
Our life on Earth,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.770
our brief little moment in time?

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:08.603
- That's something that we

00:01:08.603 --> 00:01:10.233
answer by our own activities.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.040
There's no general answer.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.230
We determine what the

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.313
meaning of it is.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.340
- The action determining meaning.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.270
- Meaning in the sense of significance.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.740
Not meaning in the sense that

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.173
chair means this.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.170
But the significance of your life

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.513
is something you create.

